Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 05:25:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 28/49] A14: backup formats a completed item's line only when
 it will be printed

Port of one hunk of T4's S016 tree (teams/T4/S016/M004,
internal/ui/backup/text.go). For every file and directory the text
progress quoted the path and formatted two or three sizes, then passed
them to VV, which prints at verbosity 3 and above only. At lower
verbosity the work had no reader. CompleteItem now returns first when
the verbosity is below 3.

Nothing printed changes: text_complete_item_test.go compares the
terminal output with a verbatim copy of stock's function at verbosity
0 to 4 for every kind of item, with names that need quoting. The JSON
progress and the counters (updated before this call) are untouched.

The other part of that tree, checker_assist.go, is a decode assistant
for check's extra worker, the lever the installed bounded check worker
already holds; it is not taken.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
